Compare an RLE block's regenerated size, not its one-byte body, with
Block_Maximum_Size.

RFC 8878 3.1.1.2.3: Block_Size is limited by Block_Maximum_Size, the
smaller of Window_Size and 128 KiB, and for an RLE block Block_Size is the
number of times its byte is repeated. ZSTD_decompressContinue(), the
streaming path, compared cBlockSize instead, which ZSTD_getcBlockSize()
returns as 1 for an RLE block: the size of its body. A single-segment frame
declaring Frame_Content_Size 0 has a Window_Size, and so a
Block_Maximum_Size, of 0, so an RLE block of size 0 in it was refused as
"Block Size Exceeds Maximum" -- a valid 14-byte frame that the zstd CLI and
the one-shot decoder accept was corrupt data when streamed a few bytes at a
time (zukomp's fuzz oracle comparing a split decode with a whole one, #68).

The regenerated size of an RLE block is still checked after decoding
("Decompressed Block Size Exceeds Maximum"); this makes the header check
measure the same quantity, so an oversized RLE block is now refused when
its header is read. Written to be upstreamable as-is.

--- a/decompress/zstd_decompress.c
+++ b/decompress/zstd_decompress.c
@@ -1312,7 +1312,13 @@
         {   blockProperties_t bp;
             size_t const cBlockSize = ZSTD_getcBlockSize(src, ZSTD_blockHeaderSize, &bp);
             if (ZSTD_isError(cBlockSize)) return cBlockSize;
-            RETURN_ERROR_IF(cBlockSize > dctx->fParams.blockSizeMax, corruption_detected, "Block Size Exceeds Maximum");
+            /* Block_Size, which RFC 8878 3.1.1.2.3 bounds by
+             * Block_Maximum_Size, is the regenerated size for an RLE block;
+             * cBlockSize is its one-byte body. Comparing that refused an RLE
+             * block of size 0 in a frame whose window is 0 (single segment,
+             * Frame_Content_Size 0) whenever the frame was streamed. */
+            RETURN_ERROR_IF((bp.blockType == bt_rle ? (size_t)bp.origSize : cBlockSize) > dctx->fParams.blockSizeMax,
+                            corruption_detected, "Block Size Exceeds Maximum");
             dctx->expected = cBlockSize;
             dctx->bType = bp.blockType;
             dctx->rleSize = bp.origSize;
